  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fourniture de services multisectoriels essentiels de Sant&#xE9;, Nutrition, WASH, Protection et Education aux populations touch&#xE9;es par les inondations dans les d&#xE9;partements de la Likouala, Cuvette et Plateaux</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health, nutrition, protection, education, and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) assistance to vulnerable communities affected by flooding. Through this project, UNICEF will provide lifesaving, multisectoral assistance to 136,000 people in the form of primary health care services, screening and treatment of SAM, safe access to water and latrines, provision of WASH kits, children protection, and emergency education. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 136,000 people, including 17,224 women, 100,000 children, and 1,518 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
